name 'pl-aif-2-U3-CFU-building-pipelines_2026'
title 'title'
description 'description here'

markdown <<MARKDOWN
## Pipeline Check: Trending Now Playlist

<div style="display:flex; gap:28px; align-items:flex-start; margin:24px 0;">

  <div style="flex:2;">

  <p style="font-size:18px; line-height:1.5;">
      A music app wants to show users a <strong>“Trending Now”</strong> playlist.
    </p>

  <p style="font-size:18px; line-height:1.5;">
      The app should:
    </p>

  <ol style="font-size:17px; line-height:1.6;">
      <li>Only include songs tagged <strong>“pop”</strong></li>
      <li>Order those songs from most plays to least plays</li>
      <li>Display only the top 5 songs</li>
    </ol>

  <p style="font-size:20px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:22px;">
      Which pipeline correctly creates this playlist?
    </p>

  <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:14px; margin:18px 0 0 0; max-width:900px;">

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer; display:block; background:#F5F7F8; padding:16px 20px; border-radius:999px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; list-style:none; box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
          sort songs by plays → filter songs with tag "pop" → take first 5
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:10px; background:#FFF4F4; border-radius:14px; padding:14px 18px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
          ❌ Not quite. Sorting first ranks all songs, including songs that are not pop. The app should filter to pop songs first.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer; display:block; background:#F5F7F8; padding:16px 20px; border-radius:999px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; list-style:none; box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
          take first 5 songs → filter songs with tag "pop" → sort by plays
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:10px; background:#FFF4F4; border-radius:14px; padding:14px 18px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
          ❌ Not quite. Taking the first 5 too early might remove pop songs that should have been considered.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer; display:block; background:#F5F7F8; padding:16px 20px; border-radius:999px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; list-style:none; box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);">
          search for "pop" → sort songs alphabetically → take first 5
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:10px; background:#FFF4F4; border-radius:14px; padding:14px 18px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
          ❌ Not quite. The goal is to filter by the pop tag and sort by plays, not alphabetically.
        </div>
      </details>

  <details>
        <summary style="cursor:pointer; display:block; background:#F5F7F8; padding:16px 20px; border-radius:999px; font-size:17px; font-weight:600; list-style:none; box-shadow:2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);">
          filter songs with tag "pop" → sort songs by plays → take first 5
        </summary>
        <div style="margin-top:10px; background:#EAF7F8; border-left:6px solid #008C95; border-radius:14px; padding:14px 18px; font-size:16px; line-height:1.5;">
          ✅ Correct. First narrow the list to pop songs, then rank those songs by plays, then take the top 5.
        </div>
      </details>

  </div>

  </div>

  <div style="flex:1; text-align:center;">
    <img 
      src="https://images.code.org/c5d1113a766b23532d5bbf0159364749-image-1779301132196.png" 
      alt="music app playlist illustration" 
      style="width:100%; max-width:260px; border-radius:14px;"
    >
  </div>

</div>
MARKDOWN
